WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:01.668
It's official.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.671
Taylor Swift is a billionaire.

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:07.424
Welcome to the Eras Tour.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:12.220
Her Eras Tour alone is a party, generating
hundreds of millions of dollars.

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:15.765
It's a multinational conglomerate
with the world's most devoted

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:19.310
customer base
and an ultra-charismatic CEO.

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:25.483
Never before have we ever seen an artist
put multiple stadium

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:29.404
shows on sale in the same city
and blow them all out.

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:33.658
But how much of the money has gone
into that CEO's pocket?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.702
We've crunched the numbers to come up

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:39.205
with the most definitive account
yet of Taylor Swift's wealth.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:41.207
And here it is.

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:45.712
Bloomberg has a team

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.715
that tallies up how much the world's
wealthiest people are worth.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.801
It's based on careful calculation
and analysis

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.804
of all their income and assets.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.433
Taylor has become a billionaire
not just because people like her songs,

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:02.562
but because of a lot of smart business
decisions that she's made over the years.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:06.483
Taylor Swift is a phenomenon,
but she's hardly the first billionaire

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:08.151
in the music industry.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.445
There's the record label scion
David Geffen, 

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:14.074
there’s Jay-Z, Rihanna, the late
Jimmy Buffett and plenty of others.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:19.621
While those billionaires use their fame
as the foundation for other business ventures, 

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:23.458
Swift has made her fortune
almost exclusively from her music.

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.586
She has really come out openly
about the importance

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.589
of controlling your music
and owning your music as an artist.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.801
So, where exactly does her wealth
come from?

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.677
Let's start with streaming.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:38.014
The rise of Spotify, Apple Music
and others has created

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:40.266
a resurgence in the recording industry.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:44.687
We estimate that her total income
from streaming is 175 million.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.441
Clearly not a number to sniff at,
but one reason it's

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.820
not bigger is because of the way
royalties are distributed.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:57.450
Typically, what happens is artists
don't own the masters of their music,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.245
but they get royalties from it.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:04.499
The owners of the masters
generally keep 4/5 of the royalties,

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:09.087
while the copyright holders, the composers
and lyricists, keep the rest.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.967
So what Taylor has done recently
and has been a very smart business

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.178
decision is to rerecord her albums

00:02:17.178 --> 00:02:20.098
and then own the masters of those.

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:23.810
So with this rerecording exercise, she's
kind of taking back control of her music.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:27.981
She's reclaiming ownership of it,
but she's also diluting the value

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.901
of the masters to the first six albums
that are originally out there.

00:02:32.193 --> 00:02:35.238
Swift also took the battle
to the streamers themselves.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:39.868
So in 2014, Taylor Swift
pulled all of her music off of Spotify.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:45.582
She did it in protest of what she said
was unfair compensation from the streamer.

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:49.252
That gave her the upper hand
when she renegotiated her rates

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:52.005
to join Spotify again in 2017.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.633
She's also done a great job in promoting
physical album sales

00:02:55.633 --> 00:03:00.471
online through Twitter, Instagram,
other social media networks.

00:03:00.471 --> 00:03:03.474
So, fans have an incentive
to buy physical records.

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:07.395
She's leveraged social media
and kind of connecting with fans,

00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:10.899
getting to know them on a personal level,
sharing information about herself,

00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:14.110
kind of creating this intimacy
which has created

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.447
this really, really powerful fan base
who connect with her.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:24.120
Bloomberg estimates Swift has made 
$125 million over the years from record sales. 

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:26.497
She also made strong strategic choices

00:03:26.497 --> 00:03:28.041
at the negotiating table.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.419
In 2018, she left her longtime

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:34.422
record label,
Big Machine, to go independent.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:38.801
She negotiated a new contract
with Universal Music Group

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:42.847
in 2018 that allows her
to take a larger share of the royalties.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:47.185
The biggest part of her earnings
is undoubtedly her concert revenue.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:52.941
Taylor Swift's concerts have generated
at least $1.6 billion,

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:55.944
and that is only ticket sales, that’s
not including merchandise.

00:03:56.486 --> 00:04:00.406
She's done six tours over the years since 2009.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.659
Most recently, the Eras Tour.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:06.621
It came right as everyone 
was starved for live events.

00:04:06.621 --> 00:04:07.997
People were coming out of the pandemic

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:11.876
and really wanted a chance
to gather in person and celebrate.

00:04:12.293 --> 00:04:13.294
And there are people

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:16.506
that are willing to spend anything
and everything to get a chance to see her.

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:19.968
A splurge, for sure. But I got to do it.

00:04:20.176 --> 00:04:22.762
We've just been trying
without mortgaging the house.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.307
Of course, she doesn't keep all of that money.

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:31.312
We estimate that Taylor nets
about 35% of the ticket sales as profit,

00:04:31.312 --> 00:04:34.607
about 500 million
from touring over the years.

00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:39.028
Her tours, her record sales and streaming
royalties are all earnings.

00:04:39.028 --> 00:04:42.115
But she also has assets,
including her recording catalog.

00:04:43.324 --> 00:04:45.743
There's the masters’ rights,
then there’s the publishing rights.

00:04:46.202 --> 00:04:50.248
Catalog is a collection of songs
all grouped under one artist.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:53.334
Every time a song in this catalog is played,

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:56.337
it generates a royalty,
which goes back to the owner.

00:04:57.088 --> 00:05:00.508
Swift doesn't actually own the first six
albums of her catalog.

00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:04.012
It's now owned by a fund 
called Shamrock Capital.

00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:06.639
She's rerecording those albums, 
meaning she'll get both

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.809
more streaming revenue
and a more valuable catalog.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.271
We estimate that her catalog is worth
about 400 million.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.024
Then, of course, there's her actual property.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.529
That includes a condo and 
an estate in Nashville,

00:05:21.529 --> 00:05:24.240
an estate in Los Angeles,  a large 

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.912
apartment in Tribeca in New York City,
as well as a summer house in Rhode Island.

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:34.292
The Rhode Island property is interesting
because it's not really a typical

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:37.253
haunt for celebrities or pop stars.

00:05:37.712 --> 00:05:41.716
It's an old world,
sort of old money part of the country.

00:05:41.716 --> 00:05:44.761
But it is kind of in keeping 
with Taylor Swift's image

00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:48.014
of the sort of girl next door,
a little bit of a homebody.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.893
In fact, she's also, has hosted
fans there in the past and

00:05:51.893 --> 00:05:54.979
baked them home-baked cookies
at this property.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:06:01.069
Making bulk batches of chocolate chip
and toasted coconut cookies.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:05.073
The total value of her properties
is about 110 million.

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:08.618
Subtract her expenses, taxes,

00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:12.038
staff costs and so on,
and you get a net worth

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:15.416
of $1.1 billion.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.795
This was a huge year

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:21.839
for Taylor Swift that tipped 
her into a new echelon.

00:06:21.839 --> 00:06:23.424
But with the 33-year-old having

00:06:23.424 --> 00:06:26.219
just set a concert film record
and the international leg 

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:30.181
of her tour getting underway,
she may only be getting started.

